{
  "requirement": "Directory groups under\n{cite}`requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.directories` MUST be expanded\ninitially in the combined gaps overview. File rows at the workspace root MUST\nremain visible.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has two obligations. The test is `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[combined_directory_minimum_includes_hidden_passing_files]`, and it covers both.\n\n1. **Directory groups expanded initially.** The test builds a three-level hierarchy: `src`, `src/nested` and `src/nested/deep`. It renders the combined overview through `populate` and isolates the map with `map_html`. It then asserts that `data-directory=\"src\" open` appears. It also loops over all three directories and asserts that each `data-directory=\"…\" open` is present. That covers nested descendant groups as well as the top-level one. `assert_directory_contents` confirms the groups really nest and hold the expected files and child groups.\n\n2. **Root file rows remain visible.** The fixture's root `code.rs` has an uncovered line from `record(..., &[(1,0),(2,1)])`, so it appears in the map. The test asserts `data-file=\"code.rs\"` is present. It also asserts that this row comes before the first `<details class=\"gap-directory\"`, so the row is not inside any directory group. `assert_eq!(map.matches(\"data-file=\").count(), 3)` checks the row count.\n\nAn implementation that rendered groups collapsed, left only the top group open, or hid or nested the root file rows would fail these assertions.\n\nThe collapse behaviour and the summaries in the parent requirement `requirements.test-coverage.index.file_map.directories` are cited context. They are not assessed here.",
